1. SUBJECT
   This agreement covers the files distributed by the Licensor as part of
   D.R.O.N.E.: the mod binary (main.dll), its configuration examples, the
   accompanying documentation, and the supplied tools (rc.py,
   befehle_testen.py, the web panel). Third-party components are governed by
   clause 8 and are not subject to this agreement.

2. GRANT OF USE
   The Licensor grants you a free, non-exclusive, worldwide right to install
   and run the software on any number of game servers, private or public.
   This expressly includes servers that finance themselves through donations,
   VIP memberships, or comparable player contributions. You may make backup
   copies.

3. RESTRICTIONS
   You may not:
   a) sell, rent, lease, sublicense or otherwise commercialise the software
      itself, nor offer it as a paid product or as part of a paid service
      (for example a paid server-setup or hosting package in which the
      software is a billed component);
   b) modify the software, create derivative works, or decompile,
      disassemble or otherwise reverse engineer it, to the extent permitted
      by applicable law. Mandatory rights under Art. 6 of Directive
      2009/24/EC and Sections 69d, 69e UrhG (decompilation for
      interoperability, error correction, backup) remain unaffected;
   c) redistribute the software outside the official release channel. Link
      to the official releases instead of rehosting them;
   d) remove or alter copyright notices, licence texts or checksums.

4. OWNERSHIP
   The software is licensed, not sold. All rights not expressly granted
   remain with the Licensor.

5. NO WARRANTY
   The software is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind, express
   or implied, including but not limited to fitness for a particular
   purpose. The Licensor does not warrant uninterrupted or error-free
   operation. The software patches a running game server process; you are
   responsible for your own backups.

6. LIABILITY
   The Licensor is liable without limitation for intent and gross
   negligence, and for injury to life, body or health. Any further liability
   is excluded to the extent permitted by law. The software is provided free
   of charge; Section 521 BGB applies.

7. TERM
   This licence terminates automatically if you breach clause 3. Upon
   termination you must cease all use and delete all copies.

8. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
